From: Jack Wen <jackwen04@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 16:03:00 -0800
Subject: [PATCH 06/10] kk: Pass clip and cull distances to a GS as they are

The stage feeding a GS runs as compute and stores its outputs to memory
for the GS to read, so it has no use for the Metal lowering of clip and
cull distances, which also separates the combined clip and cull array the
GS reads. The GS's rasterization VS lowers them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c
index eca5a6d9106..3110a8e63b5 100644
--- a/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c
+++ b/src/kosmickrisp/vulkan/kk_shader.c
@@ -1083,9 +1083,10 @@ kk_compile_shader(struct kk_device *dev, nir_shader *nir,
 
    unsigned num_cull_distances =
       prev_stage ? prev_stage->info.num_cull_distances : 0;
-   /* A GS lowers clip and cull distances on its rasterization VS instead; the
-    * stage feeding it has none after linking */
-   if (stage != MESA_SHADER_GEOMETRY)
+   /* A GS lowers clip and cull distances on its rasterization VS instead. The
+    * stage feeding it passes them to the GS in memory as they are, combined,
+    * which is how the GS reads them. */
+   if (stage != MESA_SHADER_GEOMETRY && next_stage != MESA_SHADER_GEOMETRY)
       msl_nir_lower_clip_cull_distance(nir, num_cull_distances);
 
    /* When using poly to emulate tessellation or GS, the VS and TCS are turned
